    "text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> capacitor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is first charged to a potential difference of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> using a battery. Then the battery is removed and the capacitor is connected to an uncharged capacitor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>. The charge in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> on equilibrium condition is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. (Round off to the Nearest Integer)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0094_34bbf7943d28.png\" style=\"width: 315px; height: 136px;\" /></p>"
  },
